<resources>
    <!-- Put the Device mode tile in the default Quick Settings panel.

         ── Why this and not only the home-screen widget ────────────────────
         The moment you actually want to change mode is while a game is already
         full-screen, where the launcher is unreachable and the shade is not. A
         tile that has to be dragged in from the edit screen first is a tile most
         users never find, so it may as well not exist.

         ── Which resource, and how that was determined ─────────────────────
         QSHost.getDefaultSpecs (frameworks/base/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/
         systemui/qs/QSHost.java:42-52) picks between TWO strings:

             QsInCompose.isEnabled() ? quick_settings_tiles_new_default
                                     : quick_settings_tiles_default

         so overriding the wrong one is a silent no-op. Measured which is live
         rather than guessing: `adb shell settings get secure sysui_qs_tiles`
         returns exactly AOSP's quick_settings_tiles_new_default
         (internet,bt,dnd,cast,flashlight,airplane,rotation,wallet,alarm,controls,
         screenrecord,battery), so QsInCompose is on and the *_new_default string
         is the one that matters. Both are overridden here anyway: the flag is a
         build-time read-only value that a later PixelOS merge could flip, and
         keeping the two lists in step costs one extra element.

         The custom(pkg/cls) syntax is AOSP's own — the stock default list already
         carries custom(com.android.permissioncontroller/...SafetyCenterQsTileService).

         ⚠️ This is the DEFAULT set, applied once when Settings.Secure
         sysui_qs_tiles has never been written. It does not appear on a device
         whose /data already carries a tile list; that is only reachable through a
         data wipe, which is exactly the case that matters here (first boot after
         a flash). Criterion after flashing:
             adb shell settings get secure sysui_qs_tiles
         must contain custom(org.pixelos.malbec.parts/...PenModeTileService).

         Appended at the end rather than inserted, so nothing the user expects in
         the first row moves. -->
    <string name="quick_settings_tiles_default" translatable="false">
        internet,bt,flashlight,dnd,alarm,airplane,controls,wallet,rotation,battery,cast,screenrecord,mictoggle,cameratoggle,custom(com.android.permissioncontroller/.permission.service.v33.SafetyCenterQsTileService),custom(org.pixelos.malbec.parts/org.pixelos.malbec.parts.display.PenModeTileService)
    </string>

    <string name="quick_settings_tiles_new_default" translatable="false">
        internet,bt,dnd,cast,flashlight,airplane,rotation,wallet,alarm,controls,screenrecord,battery,custom(org.pixelos.malbec.parts/org.pixelos.malbec.parts.display.PenModeTileService)
    </string>
</resources>
